ENG-15  A window smaller than the screen that goes to native full screen keeps its program's size and is scaled up.

dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_window.m (winemac.so). Lullaby, 2026-10-28. LGPL-2.1-or-later like Wine.

What: a game that runs in a window of its own size (1920x1200 chosen in its settings, a 960x600 point window on a 3024x1964 screen)
and is put into native full screen by windowstate or the green button was told by the engine its window had become the size of
the screen (windowDidResize posts the real frame), so it made a swapchain of the screen's size (Unity PEAK: 3024x1833) and, on
leaving, saved that size over the one the player had chosen. Now, when a window goes to native full screen (windowWillEnterFullScreen)
and Wine's own frame is smaller than the screen (less than the screen's width, or more than 40 points shorter than its height),
the window becomes scalable (presentationScalable, as for a window the program refuses to resize) and keeps its Wine frame: the
program is not told the new size, the stage fits its picture into the full screen (the engine's own scaler, pointer included), and
the resolution the game saved stays the one the player chose. A window that covered the screen (RE9, ETS 2 borderless) is not
touched: ENG-12 still tells it the real size. Leaving full screen (or failing to enter it) puts the window back as it was.
Requires: ENG-12 (0006), whose report it skips for such a window.
Other bases: Dormison's cocoa_window.m only.
Test: PEAK (Unity, Vulkan) saved at 1920x1200 in a window, native full screen on: HUD at 1920x1200 with the picture filling
the screen, Player.log keeps "InitializeOrResetSwapChain 1920x1200", the registry keeps 1920x1200 after exit; RE9 still 3024x1898.
Verified on: see ledger (2026-10-28).
Switch: LULLABY_FULLSCREEN_SCALE=0 (or LULLABY_FULLSCREEN_SIZE=0) as a launch option gives the old behaviour; on by default.

